WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:05.365
Pluto is a dwarf planet in the Kuiper belt, a ring of bodies beyond the orbit of Neptune.

00:05.872 --> 00:11.057
It is the ninth-largest and tenth-most-massive known object to directly orbit the Sun.

00:11.502 --> 00:19.592
It is the largest known trans-Neptunian object by volume by a small margin, but is less massive than Eris, which is denser.

00:20.181 --> 00:27.231
Like other Kuiper belt objects, Pluto is made primarily of ice and rock and is much smaller than the inner planets.

00:27.900 --> 00:32.407
Pluto has roughly one-sixth the mass of the Moon and one-third of its volume.
